# The target spelling reduces a vector of AXIS NAMES in one call, so the source
# says "sum over channel, kernel_y, kernel_x" and the reader never has to
# recover what q, u and v meant.
#
# A single name is accepted, and a vector of integer axes is accepted, but the
# combination the blocker record asks for is not. An earlier version of this
# probe tested only the single-name form and therefore reported C4 as shipped
# while the documented target line still failed; it now pins the real target.
patches : [out_y, out_x, channel, kernel_y, kernel_x] = reshape(range(72), [2, 2, 2, 3, 3])
reduce(:add, patches, ["channel", "kernel_y", "kernel_x"])
